{
  "root_cause": "The navigation controller adds a keydown listener on each results refresh without removing the previous listener, causing stale listeners with outdated currentFocus values to remain active. After refining the search, the stale listener increments an outdated focus index, leading to the wrong suggestion being activated when Enter is pressed. Additionally, the default navigation function attempts to remove itself using the outer `navigate` function reference instead of the actual listener function, which fails to clean up listeners.",
  "repair_strategy": "Ensure only one keydown listener is active at any time by detecting and removing any existing listener before adding a new one in the navigate function, storing the listener reference on the input field for proper cleanup. Also fix the default navigation function to remove the stored listener when the suggestion list disappears.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "src/controllers/navigationController.js",
      "sha256": "cb38337c041e8e0543c4f7b31666374956d6dc85011604e12ff127c9bf67ddde",
      "before": "import { closeAllLists } from "./listController";
import eventEmitter from "../utils/eventEmitter";

/**
 * List navigation function initializer
 *
 * @param {Object} config - autoComplete configurations
 * @param {Object} dataFeedback - The available data object
 *
 */
const navigate = (config, dataFeedback) => {
  // Reset focus state
  let currentFocus = -1;

  /**
   * Update list item state
   *
   * @param {Object} event - The `keydown` event Object
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   * @param {Boolean} state - Of the arrow Down/Up
   * @param {Object} config - autoComplete configurations
   *
   */
  const update = (event, list, state, config) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    if (state) {
      // If the arrow DOWN or TAB key is pressed
      // increase the currentFocus
      currentFocus++;
    } else {
      // If the arrow UP or TAB key is pressed
      // decrease the currentFocus
      currentFocus--;
    }
    // and add "active" class to the list item
    addActive(list);
    config.inputField.setAttribute("aria-activedescendant", list[currentFocus].id);
    /**
     * @emits {navigation} Emits Event on results list navigation
     **/
    eventEmitter(
      event.srcElement,
      { event, ...dataFeedback, selection: dataFeedback.results[currentFocus] },
      "navigation"
    );
  };

  /**
   * Remove list item active state
   *
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   *
   */
  const removeActive = (list) => {
    // Remove "active" class from all list items
    for (let index = 0; index < list.length; index++) {
      // Remove "active" class from the item
      list[index].removeAttribute("aria-selected");
      // list[index].setAttribute("aria-selected", "false");
      list[index].classList.remove("autoComplete_selected");
    }
  };

  /**
   * Add active state to list item
   *
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   *
   */
  const addActive = (list) => {
    // Add "active" class to a list item
    if (!list) return false;
    // Remove "active" class from all list items
    removeActive(list);
    if (currentFocus >= list.length) currentFocus = 0;
    if (currentFocus < 0) currentFocus = list.length - 1;
    // Add "active" class to the item
    list[currentFocus].setAttribute("aria-selected", "true");
    list[currentFocus].classList.add("autoComplete_selected");
  };

  /**
   * List Navigation Function
   *
   * @param {Object} event - The `keydown` event Object
   *
   */
  const navigation = (event) => {
    let list = document.getElementById(config.resultsList.idName);

    if (!list) return config.inputField.removeEventListener("keydown", navigate);

    list = list.getElementsByTagName(config.resultItem.element);

    if (event.keyCode === 27) {
      // If the ESC key is pressed
      // Clear Input value
      config.inputField.value = "";
      // Closes open lists
      closeAllLists(config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 40 || event.keyCode === 9) {
      // Update list items state
      update(event, list, true, config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 38 || event.keyCode === 9) {
      // Update list items state
      update(event, list, false, config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 13) {
      // If the ENTER key is pressed
      // prevent the form from its default behaviour "being submitted"
      event.preventDefault();
      if (currentFocus > -1) {
        // and simulate a click on the selected "active" item
        if (list) list[currentFocus].click();
      }
    }
  };

  const navigateFn = config.resultsList.navigation || navigation;
  /**
   * @listens {keydown} Listens to all `keydown` events on the input field
   **/
  config.inputField.addEventListener("keydown", navigateFn);
};

export { navigate };",
      "after": "import { closeAllLists } from "./listController";
import eventEmitter from "../utils/eventEmitter";

/**
 * List navigation function initializer
 *
 * @param {Object} config - autoComplete configurations
 * @param {Object} dataFeedback - The available data object
 *
 */
const navigate = (config, dataFeedback) => {
  // Reset focus state
  let currentFocus = -1;

  /**
   * Update list item state
   *
   * @param {Object} event - The `keydown` event Object
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   * @param {Boolean} state - Of the arrow Down/Up
   * @param {Object} config - autoComplete configurations
   *
   */
  const update = (event, list, state, config) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    if (state) {
      // If the arrow DOWN or TAB key is pressed
      // increase the currentFocus
      currentFocus++;
    } else {
      // If the arrow UP or TAB key is pressed
      // decrease the currentFocus
      currentFocus--;
    }
    // and add "active" class to the list item
    addActive(list);
    config.inputField.setAttribute("aria-activedescendant", list[currentFocus].id);
    /**
     * @emits {navigation} Emits Event on results list navigation
     **/
    eventEmitter(
      event.srcElement,
      { event, ...dataFeedback, selection: dataFeedback.results[currentFocus] },
      "navigation"
    );
  };

  /**
   * Remove list item active state
   *
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   *
   */
  const removeActive = (list) => {
    // Remove "active" class from all list items
    for (let index = 0; index < list.length; index++) {
      // Remove "active" class from the item
      list[index].removeAttribute("aria-selected");
      // list[index].setAttribute("aria-selected", "false");
      list[index].classList.remove("autoComplete_selected");
    }
  };

  /**
   * Add active state to list item
   *
   * @param {Array <elements>} list - The array of list items
   *
   */
  const addActive = (list) => {
    // Add "active" class to a list item
    if (!list) return false;
    // Remove "active" class from all list items
    removeActive(list);
    if (currentFocus >= list.length) currentFocus = 0;
    if (currentFocus < 0) currentFocus = list.length - 1;
    // Add "active" class to the item
    list[currentFocus].setAttribute("aria-selected", "true");
    list[currentFocus].classList.add("autoComplete_selected");
  };

  /**
   * List Navigation Function
   *
   * @param {Object} event - The `keydown` event Object
   *
   */
  const navigation = (event) => {
    let list = document.getElementById(config.resultsList.idName);

    if (!list) {
      // Remove the current navigation listener to avoid stale listeners
      if (config.inputField._autoCompleteNavListener) {
        config.inputField.removeEventListener("keydown", config.inputField._autoCompleteNavListener);
      }
      return;
    }

    list = list.getElementsByTagName(config.resultItem.element);

    if (event.keyCode === 27) {
      // If the ESC key is pressed
      // Clear Input value
      config.inputField.value = "";
      // Closes open lists
      closeAllLists(config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 40 || event.keyCode === 9) {
      // Update list items state
      update(event, list, true, config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 38 || event.keyCode === 9) {
      // Update list items state
      update(event, list, false, config);
    } else if (event.keyCode === 13) {
      // If the ENTER key is pressed
      // prevent the form from its default behaviour "being submitted"
      event.preventDefault();
      if (currentFocus > -1) {
        // and simulate a click on the selected "active" item
        if (list) list[currentFocus].click();
      }
    }
  };

  const navigateFn = config.resultsList.navigation || navigation;
  /**
   * @listens {keydown} Listens to all `keydown` events on the input field
   **/
  // Remove previous listener if exists
  if (config.inputField._autoCompleteNavListener) {
    config.inputField.removeEventListener("keydown", config.inputField._autoCompleteNavListener);
  }
  config.inputField.addEventListener("keydown", navigateFn);
  config.inputField._autoCompleteNavListener = navigateFn;
};

export { navigate };"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Keyboard navigation of autocomplete suggestions will correctly reflect the current filtered list, allowing users to refine search and select the highlighted suggestion with Enter, satisfying WCAG 2.1.1 keyboard operability and 4.1.2 name-role-value.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "If a custom navigation listener is provided via config.resultsList.navigation, the deduplication logic will still replace it, which could interfere with external libraries that expect to manage their own listeners.",
    "Removing and re-adding listeners may cause a brief moment where no listener is attached if an event fires between removal and addition, though this window is extremely short.",
    "Storing a private property (_autoCompleteNavListener) on the input field could theoretically conflict with other code using the same property name, but the risk is low."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "After focusing the combobox, typing 'b' should open the suggestion list.",
    "Pressing ArrowDown twice should select the first suggestion (Blackberry) as indicated by aria-selected=true on #autoComplete_result_0.",
    "Typing 'l' to refine to 'bl' should update the list to [Blackberry, Blackcurrant, Blueberry, Boysenberry] while keeping the first suggestion selected.",
    "Pressing ArrowDown after refining should keep the first selection (still Blackberry) selected.",
    "Pressing Enter should submit 'Blackberry' as the form value.",
    "ESC should clear the input and close the suggestion list.",
    "ArrowUp and ArrowDown should wrap correctly within the current suggestion list."
  ]
}
